{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A New Hope ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pumped up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "motivated; excited", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That job seminar has me so pumped up right now!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use after visiting a seminar.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "superfluous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not necessary", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The instructor implied that cover letters were superfluous.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sell yourself", "type": "name"}, {"content": "convince people that you are able to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I feel that a cover letter gives you a chance to sell yourself and explain what you will bring to the table.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "capabilities", "type": "name"}, {"content": "abilities; what you are capable of doing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The employer must be sold on your capabilities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cut to the chase", "type": "name"}, {"content": "go directly to the point", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to cut to the chase, and explain why I'm writing to them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "objectives", "type": "name"}, {"content": "goals; targets", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am customizing my cover letter explaining all the different ways that I can meet the company's objectives. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Voice with Modals", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span> when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the 'doer' of the action.  You can also use<span class=\"strong\"> modal verbs </span> in the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sometimes, something must/can/should be done by someone. It that case, we use some<span class=\"strong\"> modal verbs</span>. Remember, after a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to</span> is not necessary before the main verb. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This lesson must be practiced. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Modal verbs</span> can add meaning connected with <span class=\"underline\">suggestion</span> or <span class=\"underline\">obligation</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Here is the structure of a <span class=\"strong\">passive</span> sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"italic\">Subject + modal verb + be + past participle </span> of the main verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">All the things I learned there <span class=\"strong\">should be implemented </span>into my job search.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">The employer <span class=\"strong\">must be sold</span> on your capabilities.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">A cover letter <span class=\"strong\">has to be done</span>.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">have to be sent</span> by Tuesday.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">have/has/must</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">(to) be</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">past participle</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A cover letter</br> They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has </br>  have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be </br> to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"done.</br>sent by Tuesday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The employer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sold.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I believe a cover letter has to be done and that it is a big part of the process.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The organization should be complimented.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All the things I learned there should be implemented into my job search.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My instructor at the seminar suggested that a cover letter didn't have to be included with your r\u00e9sum\u00e9. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Future Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> .", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'll talk to you later. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I am going to send out five resumes. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm starting work on monday. </br> I'm interviewing for a job at 2 p.m. tomorrow. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Class starts at 7:00 p.m. </span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'll have to make this short.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am going to write a cover letter for a company I'm curious about called BFP.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am customizing my cover letter explaining all the different ways that I can meet the company's objectives. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "  My class starts in five minutes. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make a list of skills and experiences you have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of jobs that your skills and experience apply to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a brief introduction about yourself and why you would be a good employee.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include descriptive adjectives to describe your character. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include your list of skills and work experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The introduction should be 150 words long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have a partner review your introduction using the passive modals to give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write an introductory letter.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use descriptive language to describe my skills, experiences and character.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback to my partner using passive modals.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss future plans.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about goals and experiences related to a job.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain the steps for a job search process.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are your best qualities as a person?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What job skills do you have right now? What jobs would require theses types of skills?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 t